# Environment variables
.env

# Virtual environment folder
venv/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
# macOS
.DS_Store

# The Obsidian vault is LOCAL-ONLY and is not versioned here.
# It holds personal writing alongside the Architecture Lab notes, and a public repo is the
# wrong home for it. It stays on disk and is untracked from this commit on — back it up
# yourself, git no longer does. Never `git add -f` it back.
# NOTE: this does not remove the vault from commits made before this one; history was
# deliberately left intact. Only new content is withheld.
vault/

# Ultralytics model weights + run artifacts (downloaded locally)
yolo*.pt
*.pt
runs/
# ...but the Rehearsal Research Program's runs ARE inspectable research memory — keep them.
# `runs/` above excludes the DIRECTORY, and git will not descend into an excluded directory,
# so each location needs BOTH the directory negation and the `/**` negation.
# These moved out of the vault when the vault stopped being versioned (see below).
!research/rehearsals/runs/
!research/rehearsals/runs/**
!research/rehearsals/foundry/runs/
!research/rehearsals/foundry/runs/**
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules

# Local runtime logs
scratchpad_backend.log
scratchpad_frontend.log

# Android
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/

# Personal career/showcase materials (private — keep out of the public repo)
showcase/

# Vision model checkpoints (large; download via requirements-ml.txt notes)
models/*.pt

# WEIGHTS-001 — model weights never enter git.
# A binary committed once lives in history forever and can only be removed by rewriting it,
# so the policy is to never add one. git holds weights.manifest.json; scripts/fetch_weights.py
# provisions the actual bytes into ~/.cache (HF / torch hub) and models/.
# `*.pt` is already covered above; these close the remaining formats.
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.ckpt
models/
# ...and the same two paths with NO trailing slash. A git worktree does not get its own `models/`
# or `venv/` directory — it gets a SYMLINK to the main checkout's, and a trailing slash matches
# only directories, so git sees an untracked FILE. Committing one would put an absolute path to
# somebody's laptop into a public repo. (The same fact is why a fresh worktree reports SAM2
# UNAVAILABLE until `models` is linked: the checkpoint path resolves against the repo root, and
# the refusal is honest enough that it reads as a decision rather than a missing symlink.)
models
venv
# NOT a blanket `*.bin` — that extension is not exclusively weights, and nothing in this repo
# tracks one today. Add specific paths if a .bin weight ever appears.

# SIM-ENGINE Lane 3 — the retina's derived vector index (LanceDB).
# `region_embeddings` in Mongo is the source of truth; this directory is a rebuildable cache
# (`retina.index_rebuild()`). Memory-mapped, tens of MB and up, and regenerated rather than
# restored — it has no business in a public repo, and no history worth keeping.
# Root-anchored (`/data/`, where `default_db_path()` puts it) rather than a bare `data/`, which
# would also swallow any nested data directory someone adds later.
/data/
